      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1921, when residents secured a branch from the Detroit Post Office to serve the new village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lphistorical.org/history-news",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Suburban Motor Car Company operated in Lincoln Park from 1911 to 1913, a brief but notable chapter in early automotive history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lphistorical.org/history-news",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bill Morrison, a native of Lincoln Park, earned acclaim as an award‑winning illustrator and comic book artist, and he recently released a new piece titled “Made in Lincoln Park, MI.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lphistorical.org/history-news",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Lincoln Park Historical Museum hosts a new book, *Lost Lincoln Park*, which maps community landmarks that have changed or vanished over time.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lphistorical.org/history-news",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Lincoln Park sits between West Wyomissing and Shillington, placing it in the heart of Montgomery County’s suburban landscape.",
